mintcam (0.2.3) noble; urgency=medium

  * Port the application from PySide6 to PyQt6 so the Python dependencies come
    from the archive (python3-pyqt6, python3-opencv, python3-numpy,
    python3-pil, python3-pyzbar) instead of a virtualenv created on first
    start. This is what a Debian package requires: no code is downloaded at
    run time and the versions are the ones shipped by the distribution.
  * The /usr/bin/mintcam launcher no longer creates a virtualenv; it runs the
    system python3 with the packaged modules.
  * requirements.txt is kept for running from a git checkout, updated to
    PyQt6, and is no longer shipped inside the package.

 -- Alex Mirici <hilliedmikerano@gmail.com>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:45:00 +0200

